        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "With time, I see it more clearly.\n\nThe fact that the polls were wrong in Spain in 2016 was probably one of the greatest political strokes of luck this country has had.\n\nIf Podemos had surpassed PSOE, my party would have been condemned to irrelevance and the Spanish left would have shifted toward a populist, anti-system and eurosceptic project.\n\nI would probably be abstaining from voting today.\n\nThat’s why I’m clear about this: never again the Third Way.\nIt almost destroyed Spanish social democracy.\n\nAnd that’s why I don’t understand how the British Labour Party still trusts Starmer."
